(This mission validation document reports the quantitative accuracy and reliability of LunarSafe's deterministic hazard detection and slope characterization) Tj
T* (engine across four NASA Lunar Orbiter Laser Altimeter \(LOLA\) Digital Elevation Model \(DEM\) benchmarks. Surface slope is computed via Horn's \(1981\)) Tj
T* (third-order finite difference operator with 8*GSD stencil weighting. To guarantee landing safety under laser measurement noise, analytical first-order error) Tj
T* (propagation computes spatial uncertainty sigma_S = [sqrt\(3\)*sigma_z / \(4*GSD\)] * cos^2\(S\) with sigma_z = 1.0m vertical LOLA accuracy \(Smith et al.) Tj
T* (2010\). Candidate landing cells are evaluated against ISRO's safe slope criterion \(<= 10.0 deg\) and filtered conservatively under a 95% confidence margin) Tj
T* (\(slope + 2*sigma_S <= 10.0 deg\). All ground-truth sites demonstrate strict agreement within the <= 2.0 deg tolerance.) Tj
